{
  "id": "electrical_inductance___serial_and_parallel_connec",
  "title": "Electrical Inductance - Serial and Parallel Connections",
  "description": "Calculate electrical inductance in serial and parallel connected inductors. Choose between serial connection (L = L1 + L2 + ... + Ln) or parallel connection (1/L = 1/L1 + 1/L2 + ... + 1/Ln).",
  "type": "chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "inductance_calculator",
      "content": "Calculate total inductance for series and parallel configurations",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "connection_type",
          "label": "Connection Type",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Serial Connection",
              "value": "serial"
            },
            {
              "label": "Parallel Connection",
              "value": "parallel"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "serial"
        },
        {
          "id": "L1",
          "label": "L1 (First Inductance)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "H",
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "L2",
          "label": "L2 (Second Inductance)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "H",
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "L3",
          "label": "L3 (Third Inductance)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "H",
          "defaultValue": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "L4",
          "label": "L4 (Fourth Inductance)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "H",
          "defaultValue": 0
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "total_inductance",
          "label": "Total Inductance (L)",
          "unit": "H",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "inputs.connection_type === 'serial' ? inputs.L1 + inputs.L2 + (inputs.L3 > 0 ? inputs.L3 : 0) + (inputs.L4 > 0 ? inputs.L4 : 0) : 1 / (1/inputs.L1 + 1/inputs.L2 + (inputs.L3 > 0 ? 1/inputs.L3 : 0) + (inputs.L4 > 0 ? 1/inputs.L4 : 0))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "id": "inductance_comparison",
      "content": "Comparison of inductance values in series vs parallel configurations",
      "options": {
        "title": {
          "text": "Inductance Comparison: Series vs Parallel"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "trigger": "axis"
        },
        "legend": {
          "data": [
            "Series Connection",
            "Parallel Connection"
          ]
        },
        "xAxis": {
          "type": "category",
          "data": [
            "L1",
            "L2",
            "L3",
            "L4",
            "Total"
          ]
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "type": "value",
          "name": "Inductance (H)"
        },
        "series": [
          {
            "name": "Series Connection",
            "type": "bar",
            "data": [
              1,
              1,
              0.5,
              0.5,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Parallel Connection",
            "type": "bar",
            "data": [
              1,
              1,
              0.5,
              0.5,
              0.235
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "formula_info",
      "content": "## Formula Reference\n\n### Serial Connection (Equation 1)\n**L = L1 + L2 + ... + Ln**\n\nWhere:\n- **L** = Total inductance (henrys, H)\n- **L1, L2, ..., Ln** = Individual inductances in series\n\nIn serial connection, inductances add directly.\n\n### Parallel Connection (Equation 2)\n**1/L = 1/L1 + 1/L2 + ... + 1/Ln**\n\nWhere:\n- **L** = Total inductance (henrys, H)\n- **L1, L2, ..., Ln** = Individual inductances in parallel\n\nIn parallel connection, the reciprocals of inductances add up. The total inductance is always less than the smallest individual inductance."
    }
  ]
}